# Tree to run, named by a <BehaviorTree ID="..."> declared under thorp_bt_cpp/bt
string subtree
# Inputs seeded into the tree's blackboard before running it, as a flat json object
string json
# Blackboard keys to report back on completion. Leave empty to instead get every key the
# run added, which is handy while figuring out what a tree produces, but gives a payload
# whose shape depends on the branches the tree happened to take
string[] output_keys
---
# Whether the tree completed with SUCCESS (a tree reporting FAILURE is still a well-served
# goal; the action is only aborted when the request itself is bad, e.g. an unknown subtree)
bool success
# Values of the requested output keys, as a json object keyed by them. Scalars map onto json
# scalars and poses onto {x, y, z, roll, pitch, yaw, frame} objects; keys left without a value
# are omitted, so the caller can tell which are missing by comparing against output_keys
string json
---
